      },
      "worked": "Since $\\binom{n}{6}$ occurs, $n\\ge6$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{n!}{3!(n-3)!}+\\frac{n!}{6!(n-6)!}&=\\frac{(n+1)!}{4!(n-3)!}\\\\120+(n-3)(n-4)(n-5)&=30(n+1)\\\\(n-3)(n-4)(n-5)&=30(n-3)\\\\(n-4)(n-5)&=30\\\\n^2-9n-10&=0\\\\(n-10)(n+1)&=0\\\\n&=10\\text{ or }-1.\\end{align*}$$\n\nHere $n-3\\ne0$, so division by $n-3$ is valid. Since $n\\ge6$, $n=10$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
